# Rebase onto latest db-foundation

`db-foundation` is the integration base for ongoing work.

**When to rebase (do this without waiting to be asked again):**
- Before opening a PR, or when the user asks to sync / pull latest / continue after a pause
- Before merging locally back into `db-foundation`
- When starting or resuming feature work on a branch that diverged from `db-foundation`

**Commands:**

```bash
git fetch origin db-foundation
git rebase origin/db-foundation
```

**Rules:**
- Prefer `rebase` onto `origin/db-foundation`, not merge of `db-foundation` into the feature branch
- Resolve conflicts, re-run relevant tests, then continue
- Do not force-push unless the user explicitly asks (and never force-push `main`/`master`/`db-foundation`)
- If the branch was already pushed and rebase rewrote history, tell the user a force-with-lease push will be needed before they approve it
